      "writtenOn": "2021-07-27T21:17:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure it\u0027s necessary. With the swap, we get this:\n\nhalf4 myBlenderFunc(half4 _src, half4 _dst) {\n  _src \u003d sample(child1, _src);\n  _dst \u003d sample(child2, _dst);\n  // ... perform blend\n}\n\nWithout a swap we get this.\n\nhalf4 myBlenderFunc(half4 _src, half4 _dst) {\n  _src \u003d sample(child1, _src);\n  _dst \u003d sample(child2, _src);\n  // ... perform blend\n}\n\nI don\u0027t have any particular intuition for what the paint color should be when invoking the child FP of a blender, but the symmetry in the first case felt compelling. In practice I don\u0027t intend to write any blenders where the paint color is meaningful and I would be fine going to far as to drop the paint color entirely and force half4(0 or 1) here.",
